# Tier 1 adaptation for the Xiaomi Redmi 5 (rosy), mainline kernel.
#
# Reachable at all only because the codename now derives from the device tree:
# rosy has no Android container, so every ro.product.* property is empty and this
# directory could never be found while the codename came from getprop alone. The
# device tree says compatible = "xiaomi,rosy", "qcom,msm8953".
#
# Only the key devices are declared. Everything else - the panel geometry, the
# DPI, the GridUnit, the compositor geometry, the pixel ratio - either derives
# from the DRM connector or is already correct in the files the machine ships.
#
# The shipped nyx.conf has [module.keys] paths=/dev/input/event0, which is
# gpio-keys and nothing else: the power key is a separate PMIC input, so the
# power button never woke the screen. Derivation alone would not fix it either,
# because a shipped value outranks a derived one - deliberately, so that the
# by-path pins on the PinePhones are not replaced by node numbers. A Tier 1
# declaration is the way to say "this machine's shipped value is wrong", and it
# outranks both.
#
# By name, never by node number. From the boot log:
#   input: gpio-keys as /devices/platform/gpio-keys/input/input0
#   input: pm8941_pwrkey as .../pon@800:pwrkey/input/input1
#   input: pm8941_resin as .../pon@800:resin/input/input2
# Those numbers move: rosy's touchscreen (edt_ft5x06) does not always probe, and
# everything enumerated after a device that failed to appear shifts up by one.
deviceinfo_key_devices_by_name="gpio-keys;pm8941_pwrkey;pm8941_resin"
